workstreams.mechanism:
Add token-only state rules at specificity (0,6,2). They beat the (0,5,1) attribute rules at :44-52 and :74-82, which today beat SVG_STYLE's (0,3,1) state rules. Each is written with :is(.nt-edge,.nt-trunk), which is harmless before trunks exist, in the light order:
- :root[data-theme='dark'] .cm svg :is(.nt-edge,.nt-trunk):is(.sel,.lit) path.nt-line{stroke:var(--gold-11)};
- .added → var(--green-11);
- .removed → var(--sage-9), keeping its dash;
- .changed → var(--gold-9);
- .nt-mk-lit (last) → var(--violet-11);
- .nt-lift path.sel and .nt-lift path.lit → var(--gold-11); .nt-lift path.nt-mk-lit → var(--violet-11).
Mirror everything inside @media (prefers-color-scheme:dark) for [data-theme='system']. Literals stay only inside [stroke] and [fill] attribute selectors.

acceptance:
wire-merge-validate passes on 1,000 random orthogonal route sets and on every reference chapter layout:
- membership preserved (the union of chain members covering each route's pieces is exactly that route);
- chains orthogonal;
- no chain mixes shares or style keys;
- joins only at degree 3 or more;
- exactly one head per distinct end;
- offsets continuous from root to leaf;
- JSON equal twice.
